            "review_title": "Review at Chay Garden Xuân Thủy - Vegetarian Buffet & Tea House",
            "review_text": "Ben F\nBarnet, United Kingdom317 contributions\n0\nDisappointing\nJul 2025 • Family\nWe chose this restaurant because they advertised that they had a vegetarian buffet and we thought it would be great to be able to try lots of different dishes. However, it wasn't really a buffet in the normal sense that you experience in hotels and restaurants.\n\nThere was a small selection of appetisers and desserts in a small buffet area, but the rest of the food had to be ordered. Admittedly, you could order as many times as you wanted and so it was all you can eat, but it meant that you couldn't just sample a small bit of something as you had to order an entire dish of it. For us, this defeated the purpose.\n\nAdditionally, whilst the restaurant does close at 10pm, the buffet and ordering stops at 9pm. We booked a table for 8pm (which wasn't ready) and so by the time we sat down and they had explained the concept of the 'buffet' we had less than an hour.\n\nAltogether a rushed and disappointing experience.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nGo early.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 12, 2025",
